From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] api-impl: device identity from a device profile

android.os.Build and SystemProperties only had a few hard-coded values
(brand "google", manufacturer "HTC", everything else "unknown"), so apps saw
no real device. Read a build.prop-style profile (name=value lines, '#'
comments) from $ATL_DEVICE_PROFILE or /etc/atl/device.prop on top of the
built-in defaults; without a profile nothing changes. A distribution can
generate the profile from the device's own firmware (ro.product.*,
ro.build.*, ro.serialno, ro.hardware, ...), so Build.MANUFACTURER, BRAND,
MODEL, DEVICE, PRODUCT, BOARD, HARDWARE, FINGERPRINT, ID, DISPLAY, TAGS,
TYPE, VERSION.RELEASE/INCREMENTAL/SECURITY_PATCH, SERIAL and getprop-style
reads through SystemProperties (also via reflection) report that device.

What describes the runtime rather than the device is never taken from the
profile: ro.build.version.sdk (and preview_sdk) always reads as
Build.VERSION.SDK_INT, the API level ATL emulates for the app, and the ABI
list (ro.product.cpu.*) stays what this runtime can execute.

Also:
- Build.MANUFACTURER reads ro.product.manufacturer (default still "HTC"),
  Build.RADIO/getRadioVersion() gsm.version.baseband; new Build.getSerial(),
  SKU, ODM_SKU, SOC_MANUFACTURER, SOC_MODEL.
- SystemProperties: get(key) returns "" (not null) for unset keys and
  get(key, def) returns def for empty values, as on Android; getBoolean is
  static and understands 1/0/y/n/yes/no/on/off/true/false; getInt/getLong
  fall back to the default on garbage; hidden set() for this process.
- Settings.Secure.ANDROID_ID: instead of a constant string, 16 hex digits
  derived from a random per-installation seed (<ATL data dir>/.android_id_seed)
  and the app's signing certificate (package name if unsigned), stable across
  runs and different per signer, like Android 8+.

